WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.086 --> 00:00:04.688
- [Narrator] Gosan Abdu
Idris is a man with a mission

00:00:04.688 --> 00:00:08.052
to end child marriage, and he's
doing it with the one thing

00:00:08.052 --> 00:00:10.384
he has at his disposal:

00:00:10.384 --> 00:00:11.555
His voice.

00:00:11.555 --> 00:00:15.222
(speaking foreign language)

00:00:19.564 --> 00:00:22.717
(uplifting music)

00:00:22.717 --> 00:00:25.522
Gosan has experienced,
firsthand, the institution,

00:00:25.522 --> 00:00:28.189
which he hopes, himself, to end.

00:00:46.266 --> 00:00:49.114
Child marriage puts women at
a particular disadvantage,

00:00:49.114 --> 00:00:51.805
because they are often
removed from school.

00:00:51.805 --> 00:00:54.098
With four children,
three of them daughters,

00:00:54.098 --> 00:00:57.009
Gosan works to educate men
and women in his community

00:00:57.009 --> 00:00:58.842
against this practice.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:01.690
Gosan hosts talks.

00:01:02.755 --> 00:01:06.867
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:06.867 --> 00:01:09.047
He speaks with men about
the the disadvantages

00:01:09.047 --> 00:01:11.284
of keeping girls out of school.

00:01:11.284 --> 00:01:14.701
He talks about allowing kids, to be kids.

00:01:43.542 --> 00:01:44.846
And it works!

00:01:44.846 --> 00:01:47.554
Many people have changed their minds.

00:01:47.554 --> 00:01:52.471
Being exposed to these new
ideas has had a positive effect.

00:01:59.203 --> 00:02:01.541
For Gosan, it all comes back to family

00:02:01.541 --> 00:02:03.291
and to his daughters.

